# Docker Compose – Short Command Notes

### 1. Check Docker Compose version

```
docker compose version
```

### 2. Create project directory

```
mkdir compose-project
cd compose-project
```

### 3. Create Compose file

Run on: Debian machine.

```
nano compose.yaml
```

Add two HTTPD services:

```
services:
  web1:
    image: httpd
    container_name: web1
    ports:
      - "8081:80"
    volumes:
      - ./web1:/usr/local/apache2/htdocs:ro

  web2:
    image: httpd
    container_name: web2
    ports:
      - "8082:80"
    volumes:
      - ./web2:/usr/local/apache2/htdocs:ro
```

### 4. Create website files

```
mkdir web1 web2
echo "Welcome to Web1" > web1/index.html
echo "Welcome to Web2" > web2/index.html
```

### 5. Validate Compose file

```
docker compose config
```

### 6. Start containers

```
docker compose up -d
```

### 7. Check containers

```
docker compose ps
```

### 8. View logs

```
docker compose logs
```

Follow logs continuously:

```
docker compose logs -f
```

### 9. Test websites

```
curl http://localhost:8081
curl http://localhost:8082
```

Browser access:

- `http://SERVER_IP:8081`
- `http://SERVER_IP:8082`

### 10. Stop and remove containers

```
docker compose down
```

### 11. Rebuild and start

```
docker compose up -d --build
